# ── Cross-target matrix harness build output (Story 1.2, AC12/F-7) ─
folio-go/.matrix-build/

# ── Story 1.3's licence-check fixture module paths deliberately live
# under `example.test/` (D-1.3.8 — RFC 2606's reserved TLD, used so a
# fixture's fake module path can never collide with a real one). `*.test`
# above, meant only for compiled Go test binaries, would otherwise
# silently swallow the whole directory (and everything AC29/AC30 rely on
# being committed) — found while staging this story's commit. Un-ignore
# it explicitly.
!lint/testdata/**/example.test/
!lint/testdata/**/example.test/**

# ── WASM build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THESE ARE IGNORED ONE FILE AT A TIME ON PURPOSE, NOT BY FOLDER. It is what
# lets folio-designer/src/generated/pdfjs-assets.ts — the one generated artifact
# that is COMMITTED, so Vite keeps the PDF.js CMaps and standard fonts in its
# immutable asset graph — stay tracked while everything beside it stays out.
#
# ⚠ SINCE STORY 15.2b A NEW EMISSION IS LIVE THE MOMENT IT IS WRITTEN. The
# font-host scans (`npm run scan:font-hosts`, `npm run scan:host-fonts`) used to
# populate themselves from `git ls-files` alone, so a generated file could never
# reach them while it was untracked. They now also read
# `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, so a generated artifact with no
# line here walks straight into the scan and reds a guard its author never
# touched. `folio-designer/src/generated/font-index.ts` is the concrete case:
# its generated header comment carries a scanned font host, and only the line
# below keeps it out of the population.
#
# folio-designer/src/build-wasm.test.ts IS WHAT ENFORCES THIS. It globs the
# scripts that write into src/generated/, reads the set of paths they emit off
# their own source, and asserts every one of them is git-ignored — except
# pdfjs-assets.ts, which it asserts is tracked and names as the deliberate
# exception. Add an emission without a line here and that test reds naming it.
#
# ⚠ THE runtime/ ENTRY BELOW IS A DIRECTORY PATTERN, AND THAT CHANGES HOW IT IS
# PROBED. Measured 2026-09-05: with the directory absent from disk,
# `git check-ignore -q -- folio-designer/src/generated/runtime` exits 1 (NOT
# ignored) while the same path with a trailing slash exits 0 — a `dir/` pattern
# only ever matches a directory, and git has nothing to tell it this path is one
# until it exists. The test therefore probes directory emissions with a trailing
# slash; without it, every tree where `npm run build:wasm` has not yet run
# reports runtime/ as an unignored offender.
*.wasm
wasm_exec.js
folio-designer/src/generated/runtime/
folio-designer/src/generated/offline-assets.ts
folio-designer/src/generated/runtime-fonts.css
folio-designer/src/generated/font-catalogue.ts
# Story 16.1's family-index module is GENERATED from the COMMITTED
# folio-designer/font-index.json by scripts/build-font-index.mjs, with no
# network and no second input. The snapshot is committed; its projection is not.
folio-designer/src/generated/font-index.ts

